      ],
      "common:shortName": [],
      "common:generalComment": [
        {
          "#text": "Lumber Core Plywood, also known as Blockboard in much of Europe, uses primarily softwood lumber for the core, making it substantially lighter than veneer core plywood or MDF. It is used a great deal in the marine and aerospace industries where weight is a chief concern. Lumber Core plywood consists of a face & back veneer, then a layer of crossband veneer, with the edge-glued lumber in the center. It should be used for the bending strength and screw-hold ability. It uses thick strips of hardwood, often Basswood, glued into a larger panel and then face veneered.",
          "@xml:lang": "en"
        },
        {
          "#text": "木芯胶合板在欧洲大部分地区也称为细木工板，主要使用软木木材作为芯材，因此比单板芯胶合板或中密度纤维板轻得多。这种胶合板被广泛应用于以重量为主要考虑因素的船舶和航空航天业。木芯胶合板由正面和背面单板组成，然后是一层横带单板，中间是边缘胶合的木材。使用这种胶合板主要是为了提高弯曲强度和螺钉固定能力。它使用硬木（通常是椴木）的厚木条粘合成较大的板材，然后进行面贴面。",
          "@xml:lang": "zh"
        }
      ],
